TATARO CV Pipeline - Launch Instructions
=========================================

Prerequisites
-------------
- ROS2 Humble sourced
- xarm_ros2 workspace built and sourced
- D455 camera connected via USB

  cd /home/pooja/TATRO/TATRO_Program_files/TATARO_FirmwareV1.0/xarm_ros2
  source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
  source install/setup.bash


1. Camera Launch
----------------
Start the RealSense driver with depth alignment and sync enabled.
Run in a dedicated terminal and keep it running:

  ros2 launch realsense2_camera rs_launch.py tf_publish_rate:=0.0 enable_sync:=true align_depth.enable:=true


2. Marker Detection (standalone test)
--------------------------------------
Detects all ArUco 7x7 markers in view and draws axes + IDs.
Use this to verify markers 51, 52, 53 are visible and detected:
python3 src/computer_vision/TATARO_CV_MarkerDetection_7x7.py
  

  Press 'q' to quit.


3. Table Cropping (standalone test)
-------------------------------------
Detects markers 51, 52, 53 to establish the table frame.
Shows three windows: camera feed, masked table, warped top-down view.
Use this to verify the table boundary is correctly detected:

  python3 src/computer_vision/TATARO_CV_TableCropping_with_ARUCO_7x7.py

  Press 'q' to quit.


4. Pipeline V1.0 (full system)
--------------------------------
Phase 1: Locks the table frame using markers 51, 52, 53.
Phase 2: Continuously tracks marker 40 and outputs its pose in robot base frame.

  python3 src/computer_vision/TATARO_CV_PipelineV1.0.py

  Press 'q' to quit.

  Marker layout (5cm black pattern, 1.5cm white border):
    51 - table BOTTOM-LEFT corner
    52 - table BOTTOM-RIGHT corner
    53 - table TOP-LEFT corner
    40 - object/gripper marker (tracked in Phase 2)



5. 
./run_pipeline_with_fastdds.sh

